    tweetarticle: "British Columbia Premier David Eby and the BC Legislature have passed legislation banning the open-air consumption of illicit drugs within 15 meters of playgrounds, spray parks, beaches, and transit shelters across the province.\n\nReview David Eby on Choseno:\nhttps://choseno.com/wall/david-eby\n\nWHAT CHANGED & TAXPAYER IMPACT:\n- Enacts the Restricting Public Consumption of Illegal Substances Act statewide.\n- Authorizes municipal police and conservation officers to seize narcotics and redirect individuals who refuse to vacate child-focused public spaces.\n- Clarifies federal Section 56 exemption boundaries following intense municipal council pushback in Vancouver, Surrey, and Kelowna.\n- Establishes a $45M provincial fund expanding designated supervised inhalation and consumption health clinics.\n\nTHE DEBATE:\n- Premier, Municipal Mayors & Police Chiefs: Emphasize that families and children have the right to feel safe in public parks and community centers, establishing common-sense boundaries on public decriminalization.\n- Harm Reduction Advocates & Legal Rights Groups: Argue that pushing consumption out of public view forces vulnerable drug users into isolated spaces, increasing fatal unobserved overdose risks.\n\nNOW YOU HAVE THE SAY — CHOSENO:\nChoseno is like Google Reviews for politicians. Don't just watch decisions happen from the sidelines — now you have the say. Review David Eby's record, speak your mind, and let your fellow constituents know where you stand on his official public wall:\nhttps://choseno.com/wall/david-eby\n\nRead the full investigative report on Choseno:\nhttps://choseno.com/news/bc-premier-david-eby-enacts-strict-ban-on-illicit-drug-use-in-parks-and-playgrounds-2026-08-25\n\n#BCPoli #DavidEby #MikeFarnworth #PublicSafety #Decriminalization #Healthcare #Vancouver #Choseno",
